DTrace coverage: bhyve, Bluetooth, Mesh, active MAC policies and descriptors
==========================================================================

Scope and result
----------------
This round adds 52 probe contracts and connects 19 pre-existing declarations
to executable sites: 20 kernel contracts and 51 user-space contracts in total.
It adds 14 installed bsdinstruments profiles. coverage-seventh.json records
exact selectors, argument counts, source hashes and new/activated status.
This extends COVERAGE-FOURTH, COVERAGE-FIFTH and COVERAGE-SIXTH; it does not
replace their kernel subsystem, driver, LinuxKPI or Linuxulator coverage.

This is semantic runtime coverage, not a claim that every function is probed.
The binary census distinguishes declarations from actual linked sites.
Current tracing builds have 73 BSDBluetooth, 31 libblemesh, 11 meshd and 70
bhyve probe names, including earlier work. Remaining declaration-only names
are recorded in /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace-seventh-validation/coverage-audit.json.
They are not counted as working probes. Snapshot-disabled bhyve deliberately
omits the checkpoint/restore provider sites while retaining migration wire
and generic device-part/virtio support.

