428 distinct ATF cases across 20 programs passed, including migration
rollback, admin reset/destroy concurrency, ISO failures, mesh friendship/proxy,
configuration, discovery, Classic audio, persistence and injected I/O failures.
The probe-tap backend compiles all 18 edited runtime sources, and its regression
checks preserve all five discovery completion arguments. Two static-library
behavior/link checks and the 120 Matter tests also passed.

Reproduction uses the prepared native amd64 world and GENERIC-NODEBUG object
root. No home-directory build/repository override is used. Run from a shell
with OS permission to write /usr/obj (16 logical CPUs on this machine):
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-base.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-compile.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-modules.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-tests.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-static.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-tap.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-seventh-check.py
  make -C /usr/obj/usr/src/amd64.amd64/sys/GENERIC-NODEBUG -j16 kernel
  python3.12 tools/build/fuchsia/test-matter.py

The host has no /dev/dtrace. Offline compilation and ELF inspection do not
qualify live provider registration/firing, hardware Bluetooth/Thread traffic,
VM checkpoint/resume under a real hypervisor, kernel runtime races or overhead.
No modules were loaded, no services/VMs were started outside isolated test
harnesses, and no packages were installed/published or machine rebooted.
